<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslavia sees grain crops up on last year.</title>
<headline>Yugoslavia sees grain crops up on last year.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslavia expects to harvest around 19,000 tonnes of rye from 10,000 hectares planted in 1997, an increase of 55 percent on last year's crop, the Federal Statistics Office said in its latest report.</p>
<p>Average rye yield was estimated at 1.91 tonnes per hectare.</p>
<p>Barley output from some 132,000 ha was forecast at 349,000 tonnes, or 13 percent up on last year's crop. Average yield was seen at 2.65 tonnes per hectare.</p>
<p>Oats were sown on 72,000 ha with output forecast at 137,000 tonnes, or four percent above 1996, and average yield at 1.91 tonnes per hectare.</p>
<p>The report was based on the state of crops on June 20.</p>
<p>Wheat output has been estimated at 2.8 million tonnes, 1.3 million more than last year.</p>
<p>--Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 311 4305</p>
